      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Traditional ox yoking remains a living craft in Helena, practiced by local artisans such as Ollie Vice, echoing Mississippi’s folklife heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/helena_mississippi",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Helena emerged in the early 19th century as settlers claimed land after Jackson County’s 1812 organization, taking advantage of fertile, waterway‑adjacent lowlands.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/helena_mississippi",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The community sits on flat coastal plain terrain, lacking major rivers or lakes, a feature that shapes its humid subtropical climate.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/helena_mississippi",
